-- title:
--   Uₚ acts as an involution on toric points
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero, $p$ prime and nonzero, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the project's sense, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a nonunit of $A$; let $\Lambda$ be level data of level $N_0$ at $p$ over $A$ (the data of a structure morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,A \to$ the base, a scheme over that base with a relative group law, and bijections identifying $J_0(N_0)$-points and points of the special fibre with sections of that group scheme), subject to the project's predicate `IsJacobian`, which requires the abelian-scheme property bundle, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois-equivariance of the point bijections, compatibility of reduction, and realisation of every Hecke element by an endomorphism of the group scheme. Let $\mathcal O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, that is the corresponding object for $J_0(N_0 p)$ over the same base. The conclusion asserts, with $J_0(N_0 p)$ regarded as a module over the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{HeckeAlg} = \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ via `heckeModuleBar`, that for every $m > 0$ and every $x$ in the subgroup $\mathcal O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ generated by the toric points of level $m$, one has $T_p \cdot (T_p \cdot x) = x$, where $T_p$ denotes the polynomial generator `heckeGen` at $p$.
--
--   On the toric part of the Néron model of $J_0(N_0 p)$ at a place over $p$ (with $p$ exactly dividing the level) the operator $U_p$ coincides with $-w_p$ for the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$, hence is itself an involution; this is the classical $U_p^2 = 1$ statement on toric points. It serves to upgrade the one-sided toric Frobenius relation to a two-sided one, and is used in the derivation of the Frobenius–Hecke relation on the toric monodromy part of $J_0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_heckeGen_smul_heckeGen_smul_eq_self_of_mem_toricPts.lean

